    "title": "Listening",
    "notes": "Our dream came true in 1995, with over 96 days of the spring and summer and an expedition of 4 men undertook with they believe that they are the first and only to complete end-to-end crossing Morocco's mountains. I talk to Charles, the leader of the expedition group about the trip.\n\n Charles, how much planning on beforehand?\n\nWell, as you know I run  this walking trips on the mountains for tourists and over the years I've collected maps and other data to prepare what I called routebook for this trip. This book basicly shows the route across the mountains we took. \n\nYou actually broke records all you have, did you?\n\nYes, It was 900 mile in total and we managed to climb 32 peaks. Moreover, 3000m high, including two,  which is the highest of Africa. We went actually out to make a name for ourselves. It just happened really.\n\nWhat was weather like?\n\nIt got us right from day one and we worked pretty taken a back really to find a rain for quite a number of days and we were force to replanning our route almost from the outside. Kne of the obvious problems is the heavy snow which blocks the mountain passes. So, you have to make considerable details. When we were on way to inner, the snow forced us into the northern bypass which was new to us. We fell upon amazing high meadows, huge, gorgeous, wonderful snow cap mountains. That was how we saw every time.",
